==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:French-power-socket.jpg|thumb|right|An electrical socket.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|socket}}, {{m|enm|soket}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|soket||spearhead}}, diminutive of {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|soc||plowshare}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{m|la|soccus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɒkɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-socket.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkɪt|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mechanics}} An opening into which a [[plug]] or other connecting part is designed to fit (e.g. ''a [[light bulb]] socket'').
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[hollow]] into a [[bone]] which a part fits, such as an [[eye]], or another bone, in the case of a [[joint]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} One endpoint of a [[two-way]] communication link, used for [[interprocess communication]] across a network.
# {{lb|en|computing}} One endpoint of a [[two-way]] [[named pipe]] on Unix and Unix-like systems, used for [[interprocess communication]].

